<subsection xml:id="subsec-kuramoto-geometric-algebra-representation" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Geometric Algebra Formalization of the Kuramoto Model</title>


   <introduction>
     <p>
       We can use geometric algebra to mathematically represent and simulate the Kuramoto model.
       This turns out not to just be an exercise in flexing geometric algebra muscles, but it has potential applications
       in developing integration schemes for the Kuramoto model that outperform the more common numerical integration
       methods like rk45.
     </p>
     <p>
       In the context of this corner of :logo: <em> There and Back Again </em>, my goal is to spend time formulating these connections in a way that is meant to get
       gets my GA neurons dusted out and in shape. My hope is to find myself building a bridge in the quantum comptuing
       direction through this process. 🔮
     </p>
   </introduction>

</subsection>